<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ammishtamru II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ammishtamru II was king of Ugarit in the thirteenth century BCE, ruling as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> at the height of the city's prosperity. His divorce from a princess of Amurru, a daughter of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benteshina">Benteshina</a>, became an international affair settled by verdicts of the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudhaliya-iv">Tudhaliya IV</a> and his officials. He was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibiranu">Ibiranu</a>.</p></div>
